title separable -- the separable convolution fast path, byte-for-byte the general at a fraction of the taps, GREEN
prompt recur the loop -- read the orientation, pick up the running thread, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, keep REMEMBER single-stranded, send often, stop at custody gates
think Read KYRI + RADIANT_STYLE to write as Kyri; read REMEMBER (giant accreted lines, ASCII-clean, no mojibake), the road-ahead itineraries, and the top session logs. The thread: Season G open-media, one image module per GREEN lap, sending each; the Microkernel double-seat leads by Lindy yet its only ungated move is study, so laps grow open-media.
think Standfast first: REDS living rows all closed, released, or resting (75 custody-gated errata, 78 provisioning released). Standfast clear, no agent-closable red open.
think Crux-first choice: the convolve_n log named three siblings -- a motion-blur kernel, a separable-kernel fast path, an alpha option. Motion blur is contained by the general NxN (a special case, low crux); the alpha option is a small flag; the separable fast path is the most Lindy (an efficiency floor every large filter descends from) and the hardest-solvable (integer rounding parity is the real problem). Crux-first takes the separable path.
think The crux is provable byte-for-byte: a separable kernel K[dy][dx] = v[dy]*h[dx] runs as two 1D passes; parity with the one-pass general holds on two conditions -- DEFER both 1D divisions to a single final divide (so the integer window sum is identical: sum_dy v[dy] * sum_dx h[dx] * px = sum (v[dy]*h[dx]) * px), and the clamp-to-edge border is itself separable (clamp_x depends only on x, clamp_y only on y, so x-clamp then y-clamp equals a single 2D clamp). Two-pass = one-pass exactly, at 2*(2r+1) taps rather than (2r+1)^2 -- 66 vs 1089 for a 33x33 window.
think Built image/separable.rye in the convolve_n idiom: SeparableKernel (h/v 1D slices, radius, combined divisor, bias), guard-once-before-alloc with eight named errors, horizontal_pass keeping the raw i32 row sum, vertical_pass accumulating i64 and dividing once, alpha carried, box_blur5/gaussian5 convenience verbs. Row intermediate i32 (bound 34.5M, safe), column sum i64 (say why: generous 1D weight bound needs the range). Opening triad, >=2 invariants per fn stated positively, unqualified assert, no compound asserts, no bare memcpy, snake_case.
think Witness tools/separable_witness.rish mirrors convolve_n_witness. GREEN on the first full metal run: the two-pass 5x5 Gaussian and box mean reproduce convolve_n's one-pass output byte-for-byte on a checker AND a colored translucent field; the tap-count win asserted (66 < 1089); the Gaussian bell strictly descending + symmetric, flat held; a directional motion kernel (horizontal box, vertical identity) blurs across only leaving a vertical line sharp; 1x1 pixel held; alpha carried; QOI round-trip; eight refusals by name; conveniences equal the general verb; determinism.
obs Cleaned two selftest snags at write time: a dead `motion` kernel with a radius mismatch (removed, 5-tap id5 used) and an unused identity3_1d export (removed). No metal red -- the parity held on the first run because the arithmetic was designed for it, not debugged into it.
obs Condensed REMEMBER Now single-stranded (council rota item 11 was single-stranded, read this lap -- the card was living its own lesson): the live-edge bullet (62,361 chars) and the Git nib paragraph (13,064 chars) were a second copy of the log index. Folded both to short pointers naming only the newest rung, directing to session-logs for per-rung detail. Cairn recorded first (crux/CAIRNS.md, walk-back nib 01b4c302c9) since the condense was substantial; no fact lost (each rung's account lives in its dated log and the README module entries).
